You can of course do Sokoban and also the mines with AC 2 or 3. It
depends on many factors whether you do one or the other; AC, HP, and
melee weapon are just some factors, being accompanied by one or more
pets is another factor, as is the ability of doing ranged attacks by
either attack spells or effective missile weapons, having defensive
wands like digging, teleportation, offensive wands like sleep or cold
or dual-use wands like fire or lightning helps a lot. Other factors
are a cloak for magic cancellation (MC) to protect against special
monster attacks or whether you have magic resistance (MR) to avoid
some game spoiling traps. The difficulty of the mines especially also
depends on your alignment which is responsible whether you'll find
more or less hostile monsters there. Having a light source also
greatly increase your survivability in the mines, since you find the
stairs and objects earlier and you detect monsters earlier, and the
chance of stepping on a trap decreases (since you don't need to step
on so many squares if you see far). The problem you should be
prepared to face in the mines is that you can become surrounded; so
engraving Elbereth reliably is very helpful.

> Since this is the thread for newbie altar questions, can I ask:  are
> monks supposed to get a particular artifact in the beginning?

No, there's no preselected weapon for Monks (as is like Snickersnee
for a Samurai, e.g.). Monks can be of each of the three alignments,
so they can get (depending on theirs alignment) all the alignment
specific weapons and the unaligned weapons. Since Monks can also not
be Elfs or Orcs they also cannot get the race specific weapons as
preselected ones.

> I once got Sting, which was pretty useless to me since I go
> weaponless.

One point with daggers is that you may collect some to throw from
distance before the monsters reach you. Getting Sting is good for
Monks because they are usually restricted in daggers and can thus get
to basic weapon proficiency with daggers after you've obtained it.

